{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1010","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1010","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1010\",\"parent_revision\":\"32c4d958408abc5f9e69e6a6101d921f7b7294bb\",\"root_revision\":\"3785f2f31a0d2c14395ea0ab750b5e647a2c16170b5a04371077e8532bbf42a0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nCreating a milestone from a set of related backlog items requires three separate phases with three different tools: (1) create items one by one via backlog_add, (2) create milestone via backlog_create_milestone, (3) assign issues via github_project_setup.py in a bash loop. Wave ordering exists only in conversation text \u2014 the dispatch plan must be re-derived from scratch by /groom-milestone.\\n\\nObserved during dh-feedbackloop-meta-refactor milestone creation: 17 items created individually, issue numbers tracked manually, wave structure (6 waves with 4 restart points) designed in conversation but not captured as data. The groom-milestone step will re-derive waves via conflict analysis, ignoring the wave ordering already designed.\\n\\nWhat would make this fluid: a single flow where the user provides items organized into waves, and the system creates the milestone, assigns issues, writes the dispatch plan YAML with wave assignments, and records restart-point metadata. The wave ordering should be a first-class data artifact from the moment of creation, not re-derived later.\\n\\nPotential MCP tool: dispatch_plan_from_items(milestone, waves_dict) that takes pre-organized wave assignments and writes the dispatch plan directly.\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-22)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**Rating:** 6/10 \u2014 P2\\n\\n**Rationale:** Workflow friction, not a capability blocker. The existing three-step flow works correctly. However, the cost of the workaround is observable and significant: during milestone #2 creation (dh-feedbackloop-meta-refactor, 2026-03-22), 17 items required individual creation, issue numbers were tracked manually, and 6 waves with 4 restart points were designed in conversation but captured as prose only. The `/groom-milestone` step then re-derived wave structure from scratch, discarding the already-designed ordering.\\n\\nImpact per session: ~18 manual issue-to-milestone assignments, wave re-derivation overhead, and structural information loss (restart points designed by the user may not survive re-derivation).\\n\\nRelative to other P2 items: addresses a repeated friction point in every milestone creation session. Not blocking any current milestone. Promote to P1 if milestone creation frequency increases.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n**Blast radius:** MEDIUM \u2014 14 files touched, no breaking changes to existing flow.\\n\\n**Code changes (6 files):**\\n- `backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 new MCP tool `dispatch_plan_from_items`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 Step 9 becomes conditional\\n- `.claude/skills/create-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 document optional wave-input path\\n- `.claude/skills/group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 reference new downstream step\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/references/dispatch-plan-schema.md` \u2014 document input variant\\n- `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` \u2014 document optional fluid flow\\n\\n**Content updates (3 files):**\\n- dispatch-plan-schema.md reference\\n- local-workflow.md Phase 2 section\\n- create-milestone SKILL.md Wave Ordering section\\n\\n**No changes to:** `dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py` (reused as-is), `pyproject.toml`, CI workflows, `work-milestone` skill.\\n\\n**Unknown:** `complete-milestone` SKILL.md \u2014 not yet inspected for wave-context assumptions.\\n\\n**Risk:** New flow is opt-in. Existing create \u2192 group \u2192 groom \u2192 work path is unchanged. Integration point is well-defined: `dispatch_plan_from_items()` produces the same `DispatchPlan` shape that `work-milestone` already consumes.\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n**All dependencies exist \u2014 no blockers.**\\n\\n- `dispatch_schema` package \u2014 exists in repo; Wave, WaveItem, ConflictGroup models verified at `dispatch_schema/core/models.py` (lines 69-74)\\n- `backlog_core` MCP server \u2014 exists; `backlog_core/server.py` is the target file for the new tool\\n- `yaml_writer.write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path)` \u2014 exists and is production-ready at `dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py` (lines 63-115); uses atomic rename\\n- `backlog_create_milestone()` \u2014 exists in `backlog_core/server.py`\\n- `backlog_update(selector, milestone=...)` \u2014 exists; confirmed as the correct way to assign issues to milestones (backlog_add has no milestone parameter)\\n- FastMCP v3 registration pattern \u2014 covered by `fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator` skill\\n\\n**No external dependencies.** No new Python packages required \u2014 ruamel.yaml and pydantic are already declared in `pyproject.toml`.\\n\\n### Agents\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-22T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Implementation:** @python3-development:python-cli-architect \u2014 new MCP tool in backlog_core/server.py, conditional groom-milestone branch, test coverage\\n- **Review:** @python3-development:python-code-reviewer \u2014 code review after implementation\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-30T05:12:23Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Implementation:** @python-engineering:python-cli-architect \u2014 new MCP tool in backlog_core/server.py, conditional groom-milestone branch, test coverage\\n- **Review:** @python-engineering:python-code-reviewer \u2014 code review after implementation\\n</div>\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Primary files to modify:**\\n\\n- `backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 add `dispatch_plan_from_items` MCP tool (new function)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 Step 9 conditional branch\\n- `.claude/skills/create-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 Wave Ordering section, lines 42-80 (document input path)\\n- `.claude/skills/group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 reference new downstream dispatch step\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/references/dispatch-plan-schema.md` \u2014 document input variant alongside output variant\\n- `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` \u2014 Phase 2 optional fluid flow variant\\n\\n**Test files:**\\n- `tests/` (backlog_core test suite) \u2014 new `test_dispatch_plan_from_items` test module\\n\\n**Needs inspection before implementation:**\\n- `.claude/skills/complete-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 unknown whether it reads wave-context assumptions; inspect before finalizing scope\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type:** unbounded-design\\n**Analysis method:** design-framing\\n\\nThe real gap is that `/groom-milestone` always re-derives wave assignments from dependency analysis, even when the user has already organized items into waves during milestone creation. The `dispatch_schema` Wave and WaveItem models are first-class data \u2014 the schema already supports pre-assigned waves. What is missing is a pathway to accept pre-organized wave assignments and write the dispatch plan directly, bypassing re-derivation.\\n\\nThis is a **workflow fluidity gap**, not a data structure gap. The current three-step flow (create items \u2192 create milestone \u2192 groom) has no handoff point where user-provided wave ordering can enter as structured data. Wave assignments designed in conversation are lost before `/groom-milestone` runs.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n**Observable when done:**\\n\\n1. Calling `dispatch_plan_from_items(milestone=2, waves={0: [1003, 986], 1: [994, 1000, 999]})` creates a dispatch plan YAML at the expected path with exactly those wave assignments \u2014 wave 0 contains issues 1003 and 986, wave 1 contains issues 994, 1000, and 999.\\n\\n2. Running `/dh:groom-milestone` on a milestone that already has a dispatch plan (created via `dispatch_plan_from_items`) results in Step 9 being skipped \u2014 no re-derivation occurs, no wave assignments are overwritten.\\n\\n3. Running `/dh:work-milestone` after step 2 succeeds without modification \u2014 the pre-created dispatch plan is consumed identically to a groom-milestone-generated plan.\\n\\n4. Running the existing three-step flow (create \u2192 group \u2192 groom without pre-provided waves) continues to work exactly as before \u2014 Step 9 derivation runs normally when no pre-provided plan exists.\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\n**What changes:**\\n- New MCP tool: `dispatch_plan_from_items(milestone_number: int, waves_dict: dict) -> DispatchPlan` in `backlog_core/server.py`\\n- `/dh:groom-milestone` Step 9 \u2014 add conditional: if dispatch plan already exists (pre-provided), skip dependency analysis and write plan directly; otherwise run existing derivation logic\\n- Optional `--waves` argument handling in `/dh:create-milestone` and `/dh:group-items-to-milestone` skills\\n- Test coverage: new unit tests for `dispatch_plan_from_items`, integration test for end-to-end variant flow\\n\\n**What stays unchanged:**\\n- Existing create \u2192 group \u2192 groom \u2192 work flow remains intact and is the default path\\n- `dispatch_schema` Wave/WaveItem/ConflictGroup models \u2014 no schema changes needed\\n- `yaml_writer.write_dispatch_plan()` \u2014 reused as-is\\n- `backlog_create_milestone()` and `backlog_update(milestone=...)` \u2014 no changes\\n- `work-milestone` skill \u2014 reads the same DispatchPlan shape regardless of how it was created\\n\\n**What is optional (deferred to implementation decision):**\\n- User-invocable skill for wave intake (can be JSON argument or interactive guide \u2014 implementation team decides)\\n\\n### Skills\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-22T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator` \u2014 MCP tool registration patterns for the new `dispatch_plan_from_items` tool in backlog_core\\n- `python3-development:python3-development` \u2014 Python implementation standards, testing, and type checking\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-30T05:12:28Z</sub>\\n\\n- `fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator` \u2014 MCP tool registration patterns for the new `dispatch_plan_from_items` tool in backlog_core\\n- `python-engineering:python3-development` \u2014 Python implementation standards, testing, and type checking\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **fluid milestone creation \u2014 create items, group, and assign waves in one flow** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 milestone #2 creation process 2026-03-22\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Rt-Ica Final Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-22T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Goal:** Enable creating a milestone with pre-organized wave assignments in one flow, writing the dispatch plan YAML directly instead of re-deriving it.\\n\\n### Condition Resolution Summary\\n\\n| Condition | Snapshot Status | Resolution Method | Final Status | Citation |\\n|-----------|-----------------|-------------------|--------------|----------|\\n| 1. backlog_create_milestone MCP tool interface | AVAILABLE | Fact-checker verified | \u2705 AVAILABLE | backlog_core/server.py |\\n| 2. dispatch_schema write_dispatch_plan function | DERIVABLE | Fact-checker verified file exists | \u2705 AVAILABLE | dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py lines 63-115 |\\n| 3. backlog_add batch capability | AVAILABLE | backlog_add creates items one at a time, returns issue number | \u2705 AVAILABLE | backlog_core/server.py |\\n| 4. GitHub issue set-milestone interface | AVAILABLE | github_project_setup.py issue set-milestone tested in dh-feedbackloop-meta-refactor session | \u2705 AVAILABLE | github_project_setup.py (tested 2026-03-22) |\\n| 5. Dispatch plan YAML schema for wave assignments | DERIVABLE | Fact-checker verified Wave, WaveItem, ConflictGroup models exist | \u2705 AVAILABLE | dispatch_schema/core/models.py (Wave class with `wave: int`, `parallel: bool`, `items: list[WaveItem]`) |\\n| 6. backlog_add milestone parameter | DERIVABLE | Fact-checker refuted: backlog_add signature has NO milestone param; uses backlog_update(selector, milestone=...) instead | \u274c NOT AVAILABLE | backlog_core/server.py async def backlog_add() signature |\\n| 7. User's desired interface for wave groupings | MISSING | Inferred from issue description: waves as dict mapping wave_number to issue lists (e.g., `{1: [#100, #101], 2: [#102, #103]}`) | \u2705 INFERRED & AVAILABLE | Issue description \u00a7 \\\"What would make this fluid\\\" |\\n\\n### Availability Count\\n\\n- **AVAILABLE**: 6 (conditions 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7)\\n- **NOT AVAILABLE**: 1 (condition 6 \u2014 but it is NOT NEEDED; backlog_update(milestone=...) fills the same role)\\n- **MISSING (at code level) but INFERRABLE from specification**: 1 (condition 7 \u2014 user interface format)\\n\\n### Decision Gate\\n\\n**All conditions are either available or inferrable from existing specifications.** The missing tool `dispatch_plan_from_items(milestone_number: int, waves_dict: dict) -> DispatchPlan` is a NEW IMPLEMENTATION, not a missing precondition. The specification is complete enough to begin design and implementation.\\n\\n### Fact-Check Refinements\\n\\nFact-checker made a critical refinement to the issue diagnosis:\\n\\n**Original claim (refuted):** \\\"dispatch plan must be re-derived from scratch by /groom-milestone\\\"\\n\\n**Fact-checker finding:** The skill DOES re-derive wave assignments from dependency analysis \u2014 but this is a design choice, not a data structure limitation. The Wave model itself is first-class data; groom-milestone simply doesn't accept pre-populated wave inputs.\\n\\n**Impact on this feature:** The feature request is NOT about fixing missing data structures (which already exist). It is about **optionally skipping re-derivation when the user provides wave assignments in advance**. groom-milestone Step 9 will become conditional:\\n- IF waves are pre-provided \u2192 skip derivation, write plan directly\\n- ELSE \u2192 perform dependency analysis, derive waves, write plan\\n\\n### Scope Clarity\\n\\n**What exists:**\\n- Wave and WaveItem models in dispatch_schema\\n- yaml_writer.write_dispatch_plan() function that persists Wave data to YAML\\n- backlog_create_milestone() and backlog_update(milestone=...) for milestone/issue CRUD\\n\\n**What must be built:**\\n- New MCP tool `dispatch_plan_from_items(milestone_number: int, waves_dict: dict) \u2192 DispatchPlan` in backlog_core/server.py\\n- Conditional Step 9 in groom-milestone skill (check for pre-provided dispatch plan)\\n- Optional --waves argument in create-milestone and group-items-to-milestone skills\\n- Test coverage for new tool and conditional workflow variant\\n\\n**What is optional:**\\n- Skill for user intake of wave structure (can be JSON arg or interactive guide \u2014 user choice during implementation)\\n\\n### Completeness Assessment\\n\\n**APPROVED FOR DESIGN & IMPLEMENTATION**\\n\\nAll information needed to begin work is present:\\n- Fact-check resolved all disputed claims\\n- Code search confirmed dispatch_plan_from_items does not exist (new tool to build)\\n- User's desired interface is explicit (dict format)\\n- Impact Radius identified all affected files and change scope\\n- Integration points are clear (MCP tool \u2192 skill conditional \u2192 write_dispatch_plan)\\n\\n### Condition Transition Snapshot \u2192 Final\\n\\n```\\nSnapshot: 3 AVAILABLE, 3 DERIVABLE, 1 MISSING\\nFinal:    6 AVAILABLE, 0 DERIVABLE, 0 MISSING + 1 tool for new implementation\\n\\nStatus progression:\\n- Conditions 1, 3, 4: AVAILABLE \u2192 \u2705 AVAILABLE (no change)\\n- Condition 2: DERIVABLE \u2192 \u2705 AVAILABLE (fact-checker verified file exists with production-ready function)\\n- Condition 5: DERIVABLE \u2192 \u2705 AVAILABLE (fact-checker verified Wave/WaveItem models with required fields)\\n- Condition 6: DERIVABLE \u2192 \u274c NOT AVAILABLE (fact-checker refuted milestone param in backlog_add; substitute: backlog_update(milestone=...))\\n- Condition 7: MISSING \u2192 \u2705 INFERRED (user explicitly stated desired input format in issue description; can proceed with design)\\n```\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code Producers (MCP Tools & Writers)\\n\\n**New Tool Required:**\\n- `backlog-core/server.py` \u2014 ADD `dispatch_plan_from_items(milestone_number: int, waves_dict: dict) -> DispatchPlan`\\n  - Input: milestone number, pre-organized wave assignments with issue numbers\\n  - Output: DispatchPlan object ready for writing\\n  - Scope: New MCP tool; registers in FastMCP server configuration\\n\\n**Modified Existing:**\\n- `dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py` \u2014 `write_dispatch_plan()` already exists and is production-ready (tested, atomic rename)\\n- `backlog_create_milestone()` \u2014 existing, no code change needed\\n\\n### Code Consumers (Skills that call writers)\\n\\n**Modified Skills:**\\n- `.claude/skills/create-milestone/SKILL.md` (lines 42\u201380: \\\"Wave Ordering\\\" section) \u2014 Already has placeholder flowchart for wave planning. Will become a documented input path. No implementation changes required.\\n- `.claude/skills/group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 No change needed; assigns to milestone. New flow will call downstream BEFORE groom-milestone.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 Step 9 calls `write_dispatch_plan()`. Will become conditional: skip if dispatch plan already provided in args.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 Reads dispatch plan from Step 4 of groom-milestone. No change needed.\\n\\n**Entry Point Skills (User-visible workflow):**\\n- `/dh:create-milestone` \u2014 WILL CHANGE: accepts optional wave assignments argument (e.g., `/create-milestone {title} --waves '{json_dict}'`)\\n- `/dh:group-items-to-milestone` \u2014 WILL CHANGE: accepts optional wave assignments in return (routes to optional dispatch plan creation step)\\n\\n### Documentation & References\\n\\n**Will Become Stale:**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/references/dispatch-plan-schema.md` \u2014 Currently documents dispatch plan as OUTPUT OF groom-milestone. Will need to document it as optional INPUT.\\n- `.claude/rules/local-workflow.md` \u00a7 \\\"Phase 2: Execution\\\" \u2014 Documents three-step process (create items, create milestone, assign). Will need to document optional one-step fluid variant.\\n\\n**Will Need New Content:**\\n- New skill: `dispatch_plan_from_items` reference doc (if exposing as user-invocable) OR internal reference (if MCP-only)\\n- Orchestration guide addendum for wave-assignment input format (JSON, YAML preview)\\n- Schema amendment: how to pre-populate `conflict-groups` and `waves` in milestone creation input\\n\\n### Configuration & CI\\n\\n**No changes to:**\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2014 No new file types\\n- `pyproject.toml` \u2014 Existing dependencies (ruamel.yaml, pydantic) are sufficient\\n- GitHub Actions workflows \u2014 No CI gate changes needed\\n\\n**May need:**\\n- Update dispatch_schema test coverage for `dispatch_plan_from_items()` (backlog_core server tests)\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n**Agent Frontmatter Changes:**\\n- `@dh:swarm-task-planner` \u2014 May need skill loading of dispatch_schema to demonstrate wave output format\\n- `@dh:context-gathering` \u2014 May need to extract pre-ordered wave info from milestone descriptions\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n**Affected Systems:**\\n\\n| System | File | Component | Q1:Break? | Q2:Stale? | Q3:Code Change? | Q4:Content Update? | Q5:Test Coverage? |\\n|--------|------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------------|-------------------|-------------------|\\n| Backlog MCP Server | backlog_core/server.py | Add dispatch_plan_from_items tool | YES \u2014 new arg, new return shape | NO | YES \u2014 new function | YES \u2014 docstring | YES \u2014 needs test_dispatch_plan_from_items |\\n| Dispatch Schema | dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py | write_dispatch_plan (reuse) | NO | NO | NO | NO | YES \u2014 existing coverage |\\n| Create Milestone Skill | .claude/skills/create-milestone/SKILL.md | wave ordering section | NO \u2014 optional feature | NO \u2014 section already exists | NO \u2014 planning only | PARTIAL \u2014 clarify intake | NO \u2014 new path untested |\\n| Group Items Skill | .claude/skills/group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md | issue assignment | NO | NO | NO | PARTIAL \u2014 reference new path | NO \u2014 integration point |\\n| Groom Milestone Skill | plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md | Step 9: dispatch plan creation | YES \u2014 conditional on input | YES \u2014 assumes derivation | YES \u2014 add conditional branch | YES \u2014 document input case | YES \u2014 needs variant coverage |\\n| Work Milestone Skill | plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md | Step 4: plan reader | NO | NO | NO | NO | YES \u2014 existing coverage |\\n| Dispatch Plan Schema Doc | plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/references/dispatch-plan-schema.md | describes plan structure | NO | YES \u2014 assumes output-only | NO | YES \u2014 add input variant | NO |\\n| Local Workflow Guide | .claude/rules/local-workflow.md | Phase 2 execution description | YES \u2014 3-step process will have variant | YES \u2014 omits optional path | NO | YES \u2014 document optional variant | NO |\\n| Complete Milestone Skill | .claude/skills/complete-milestone/SKILL.md | (if reads milestone context) | UNKNOWN \u2014 needs inspection | UNKNOWN | UNKNOWN | UNKNOWN | UNKNOWN |\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] MCP tool `dispatch_plan_from_items` defined in backlog_core/server.py with full docstring and error handling\\n- [ ] Tool integrated into FastMCP server and registered in MCP configuration\\n- [ ] Dispatch schema models (Wave, WaveItem, ConflictGroup) can accept pre-populated instances from tool input\\n- [ ] yaml_writer.write_dispatch_plan() tested with tool-generated DispatchPlan instances\\n- [ ] `/dh:create-milestone` SKILL.md updated to document optional wave-assignment input path (guided intake or JSON arg)\\n- [ ] `/dh:group-items-to-milestone` SKILL.md updated to document dispatch plan generation option after issue assignment\\n- [ ] `/dh:groom-milestone` SKILL.md updated: Step 9 becomes conditional (if dispatch plan provided, skip derivation; otherwise derive)\\n- [ ] dispatch-plan-schema.md reference updated: documents both \\\"derived\\\" and \\\"provided\\\" input modes\\n- [ ] .claude/rules/local-workflow.md Phase 2 updated: documents optional one-step flow and its preconditions\\n- [ ] New test suite: test_dispatch_plan_from_items covering wave mapping, conflict group handling, validation\\n- [ ] Integration test: create milestone \u2192 assign items \u2192 generate dispatch plan \u2192 work milestone (end-to-end variant flow)\\n- [ ] Agent instructions clarified: when swarm-task-planner receives pre-ordered items, it validates wave structure instead of deriving it\\n- [ ] Complete Milestone Skill inspected and any wave-context assumptions documented\\n\\n### Impact Summary\\n\\n**Blast Radius:** 6 files will need code changes; 3 will need content updates; 8 will become stale without updates.\\n\\n**Risk Level:** MEDIUM\\n- No breaking changes to existing flow (create \u2192 group \u2192 groom \u2192 work remains intact)\\n- New flow is opt-in (pre-organized waves are optional input)\\n- Existing dispatch plan derivation logic (groom-milestone) becomes conditional, not replaced\\n- Integration point is well-defined: dispatch_plan_from_items() MCP tool produces same DispatchPlan shape that work-milestone consumes\\n\\n**Recommended Gating:** Require end-to-end integration test before shipping. Test should demonstrate: (1) create milestone with wave descriptions, (2) assign items to milestone, (3) call dispatch_plan_from_items with pre-organized waves, (4) verify output matches expected dispatch plan, (5) feed to work-milestone and execute successfully.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-22T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| codebase-analysis | plan/codebase/milestone-creation-patterns.md | current | codebase-analyzer | 2026-03-22T15:54:46.359600+00:00 |\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-fluid-milestone-creation.md | current | feature-researcher | 2026-03-22T15:55:19.323807+00:00 |\\n| architect | plan/architect-fluid-milestone-creation.md | current | python-cli-design-spec | 2026-03-22T16:02:48.012437+00:00 |\\n| task-plan | plan/P1010-fluid-milestone-creation.yaml | current | swarm-task-planner | 2026-03-24T16:19:14Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fact-Check Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-22T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claims verified**: 6 total\\n- **VERIFIED**: 3 claims\\n- **REFUTED**: 2 claims  \\n- **INCONCLUSIVE**: 1 claim (behavioral, not schema-level)\\n\\n### Per-Claim Details\\n\\n**Claim 1: \\\"Creating a milestone requires three separate phases with three different tools\\\"**\\n- Status: **VERIFIED**\\n- Evidence: \\n  - `backlog_add` MCP tool (phase 1: create items individually)\\n  - `backlog_create_milestone` MCP tool (phase 2: create milestone)\\n  - `github_project_setup.py` bash script (phase 3: assign issues via loop)\\n  - No single combined interface exists combining all three phases\\n- Source: backlog_core/server.py, groom-milestone SKILL.md lines 84-90\\n\\n**Claim 2: \\\"dispatch plan must be re-derived from scratch by /groom-milestone\\\"**\\n- Status: **REFUTED**\\n- Evidence:\\n  - groom-milestone SKILL.md describes workflow with Step 8 (Priority Ordering) and Step 9 (Build Dispatch Plan)\\n  - These steps build the plan AFTER analyzing the actual items (dependency analysis, conflict grouping)\\n  - The skill accepts a milestone number with pre-assigned items (entry condition: \\\"at least one item assigned to the milestone via `/group-items-to-milestone`\\\")\\n  - However, wave assignments are NOT pre-accepted as input \u2014 the skill derives them by analyzing dependencies and conflicts\\n  - Distinction: items are pre-grouped into milestone, but wave assignments within that milestone are derived\\n- Source: groom-milestone SKILL.md lines 16-31 (entry conditions), lines 63-77 (dependency analysis, conflict grouping, wave assignment)\\n\\n**Claim 3: \\\"wave ordering exists only in conversation text\\\"**\\n- Status: **REFUTED (at schema level)**\\n- Evidence:\\n  - dispatch_schema/core/models.py defines Wave and WaveItem classes (lines 69-74)\\n  - Wave model has fields: `wave` (int), `parallel` (bool), `items` (list[WaveItem])\\n  - WaveItem has fields: `title`, `issue`, `priority`, `conflict_group`, `depends_on`, `status`\\n  - dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py has `write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path)` function (lines 63-115)\\n  - Function writes DispatchPlan model (which contains Wave objects) directly to YAML via ruamel.yaml\\n  - Wave ordering is a first-class data artifact in the schema, persisted to YAML\\n- Source: dispatch_schema/core/models.py lines 69-75, dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py lines 63-115\\n\\n**Claim 4: \\\"17 items created individually, issue numbers tracked manually\\\"**\\n- Status: **VERIFIED (direct observation)**\\n- Evidence: Session observation \u2014 dh-feedbackloop-meta-refactor milestone creation 2026-03-22\\n- Source: User's session notes, session observation baseline\\n\\n**Claim 5: \\\"dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py has a function that accepts pre-organized wave assignments\\\"**\\n- Status: **INCONCLUSIVE (semantic disagreement)**\\n- Evidence:\\n  - Function `write_dispatch_plan(plan: DispatchPlan, path: Path)` exists (line 63)\\n  - It accepts a DispatchPlan model that CONTAINS Wave objects with assignments\\n  - However, the function does NOT CONSTRUCT wave assignments \u2014 it receives them already-constructed in the DispatchPlan\\n  - The assignment logic is in groom-milestone skill (Step 8-9), not in the writer\\n  - The claim asks \\\"does writer accept pre-organized assignments\\\" \u2014 YES, it does (argument: plan)\\n  - But claiming the writer \\\"accepts pre-organized wave assignments\\\" conflates two separate concerns: the writer (serialization) vs the planner (assignment logic)\\n- Source: dispatch_schema/writers/yaml_writer.py lines 63-115, groom-milestone SKILL.md lines 75-77\\n\\n**Claim 6: \\\"backlog_add MCP tool has a milestone parameter\\\"**\\n- Status: **REFUTED**\\n- Evidence:\\n  - backlog_add signature (from server.py):\\n    ```python\\n    async def backlog_add(\\n        title, priority, description, \\n        source=\\\"Not specified\\\", type_=\\\"Feature\\\", \\n        create_issue=True, force=False\\n    )\\n    ```\\n  - No `milestone` parameter exists\\n  - Milestone assignment is a separate operation via `backlog_update(selector=..., milestone=...)`\\n- Source: backlog_core/server.py, async def backlog_add() signature\\n\\n### Key Finding\\n\\nThe issue description contains a **critical mischaracterization**: it states wave ordering is \\\"re-derived\\\" and \\\"not captured as data,\\\" but the schema and writer demonstrate waves ARE first-class data artifacts. The real problem is **process fluidity**, not data structure:\\n\\n- Current flow: Create items \u2192 Create milestone \u2192 Group items \u2192 Run groom-milestone (which re-analyzes dependencies/conflicts and derives wave assignments)\\n- Desired flow: Create items with wave pre-assignments \u2192 Create milestone \u2192 Write dispatch plan directly (skipping re-derivation)\\n\\nThis is different from what #1010 claims. The data structure already supports wave assignments; the issue is that `/groom-milestone` doesn't accept or preserve user-provided wave groupings \u2014 it always re-analyzes and re-assigns.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"83a1bd9c91203d90eaed25b6a6e36bab594a0862bca695b770296f75be40c2bd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTb6qA\"}"}